  "summary": "Several significant developments are reshaping healthcare delivery and policy today. Amylyx Pharmaceuticals reported pivotal trial success for avexitide, a GLP-1 antagonist for post-bariatric hypoglycemia, achieving a 55% reduction in serious low blood sugar events and planning an FDA filing. Meanwhile, administrative challenges are mounting across the sector: the Trump administration faces legal challenges over visa restrictions affecting foreign graduate students and postdocs in medical research, while government workers and municipalities are struggling with surging health insurance costs that are forcing difficult decisions on benefits and taxes. On the technology front, workflow accountability in healthcare AI is emerging as a critical focus area as implementation accelerates, while the FTC's potential antitrust probe into Epic has prompted the healthcare software giant to respond, and data interoperability initiatives are expanding through increased ONC funding for TEFCA and new app libraries enabling patient health data exchange. Finally, a government official with ties to the NIH pleaded guilty to avoiding public records requests while advancing private company interests, adding to scrutiny over conflicts of interest in health policy.",
